{
  "id": "higher-order-conditioning",
  "term": "higher order conditioning",
  "definition": "Higher-order conditioning is a form of classical conditioning in which a new stimulus becomes conditioned by being paired with another conditioned stimulus rather than being paired directly with the original event. In the packet’s example, geometric figures were linked to smoking-related or neutral stimuli so they could acquire conditioned responses indirectly.",
